{"authored" [{"question" "q-127742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${B}^{-1}$, where \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $B$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(B)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(B)=2\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 1=-1\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(B)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-1)}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B{B}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {B}^{-1}B & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813d2525e7300acba1c5741f8f251e0c556c58d8bdbd4e492941c9e96ab90782" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 6 \\\\ 10 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,Y=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,Z=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- The matrix $X$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $Y$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Y)=6\\cdot 6-7\\cdot 5=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Y)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $Y$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $Z$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Z)=(-2)\\cdot 5-10\\cdot 1=-20.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Z)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $Z$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $X$ does not have an inverse." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813d2525e7300acba1c5741f8f251e0c556c58d8bdbd4e492941c9e96ab90782" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$X$ and $Y$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$X$ and $Z$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$X$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$Y$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$Z$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$X$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/state.json" "file_sha256" "6eec2d798dc7f5a72f06bc5a6741714b2bc2facc2c86f711dc7387c957724ae9" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $A^{-1},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/example-4502.json" "file_sha256" "d90d1dc48691d5c8e6cd79aaa9450e15416a1c0437b2e49a41de506ae4054a06" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a $2 \\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $A$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\det(A) = 1 \\cdot 1 - 0 \\cdot (-2) = 1\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}]. \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -0 \\\\ -(-2) & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{A}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {A}^{-1}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/example-4502.json" "file_sha256" "d90d1dc48691d5c8e6cd79aaa9450e15416a1c0437b2e49a41de506ae4054a06" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4503" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/example-4503.json" "file_sha256" "c5231f1b59cd38e29c467d9e0c7ea837116f3d696d9cd56f0255d2f4b94f850c" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4503" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the matrix $A$, we have\n\n$$\n\\det({A})=1 \\cdot 1 - 1 \\cdot 1 = 0.\n$$\n\nBecause $\\det(A)=0,$ we conclude that $A$ is not invertible. Since $A$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $A$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\n\\det({C})=3 \\cdot 3 - (-3) \\cdot 3 = 18.\n$$\n\nBecause $\\det(C) \\neq 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is singular." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/example-4503.json" "file_sha256" "c5231f1b59cd38e29c467d9e0c7ea837116f3d696d9cd56f0255d2f4b94f850c" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If \n$[\\begin{aligned}1-k & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1-k\\end{aligned}]$\n is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/example-4504.json" "file_sha256" "34fa14c36f2c4f3a517ce126819d1d70167f169e288fc03290cd6aa8867b1cee" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $\\det(A)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =(1-k)(1-k)-4 \\\\  & ={k}^{2}-2k-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $k\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{k}^{2}-2k-3 & =0 \\\\ (k-3)(k+1) & =0 \\\\ k & =3,-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $k$ are $k=3$ and $k=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/example-4504.json" "file_sha256" "34fa14c36f2c4f3a517ce126819d1d70167f169e288fc03290cd6aa8867b1cee" "basis" 766 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975082/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11718" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ea4311d42424461cce7ae9887645fdf161846a413965216c517a96ebc1690e" "basis" 1228 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11718" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the matrix $A$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 1=-1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(A)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=1\\cdot 0-0\\cdot 1=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)=0,$ we conclude that $C$ is not invertible. Since $C$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $C$ is singular.\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is singular." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ea4311d42424461cce7ae9887645fdf161846a413965216c517a96ebc1690e" "basis" 1228 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11718" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6dfec28172520e24dfb5fac9e6d1db42228096620e675745f931faa32c6d1a6" "basis" 1228 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11718" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ea4311d42424461cce7ae9887645fdf161846a413965216c517a96ebc1690e" "basis" 1228 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11718" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ and $B$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ea4311d42424461cce7ae9887645fdf161846a413965216c517a96ebc1690e" "basis" 1228 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11718" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ and $C$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ea4311d42424461cce7ae9887645fdf161846a413965216c517a96ebc1690e" "basis" 1228 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11718" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$B$ and $C$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ea4311d42424461cce7ae9887645fdf161846a413965216c517a96ebc1690e" "basis" 1228 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11718" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$B$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ea4311d42424461cce7ae9887645fdf161846a413965216c517a96ebc1690e" "basis" 1228 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11718" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$C$ only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ea4311d42424461cce7ae9887645fdf161846a413965216c517a96ebc1690e" "basis" 1228 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11718" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$C$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ea4311d42424461cce7ae9887645fdf161846a413965216c517a96ebc1690e" "basis" 1228 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3x+2 & 2x-4\\end{aligned}]$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ea4311d42424461cce7ae9887645fdf161846a413965216c517a96ebc1690e" "basis" 1228 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =1\\cdot (2x-4)-2\\cdot (3x+2) \\\\  & =2x-4-6x-4 \\\\  & =-4x-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x-8 & =0 \\\\ -4x & =8 \\\\ x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ea4311d42424461cce7ae9887645fdf161846a413965216c517a96ebc1690e" "basis" 1228 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6dfec28172520e24dfb5fac9e6d1db42228096620e675745f931faa32c6d1a6" "basis" 1228 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316782" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ea4311d42424461cce7ae9887645fdf161846a413965216c517a96ebc1690e" "basis" 1228 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-127742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${B}^{-1}$, where \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-127742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $B$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(B)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(B)=2\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 1=-1\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(B)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-1)}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B{B}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {B}^{-1}B & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-127742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5afafdb2e5d49013b9bae6603b0bcc9b16798670b03dcd72532f109953042af6"} {"question" "q-127742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-127742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-127742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-7945" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${Q}^{-1}$, where\n$Q=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-7945" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $Q$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(Q)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(Q)=(-3)\\cdot (-2)-5\\cdot 1=1\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(Q)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q{Q}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {Q}^{-1}Q & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-7945" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5afafdb2e5d49013b9bae6603b0bcc9b16798670b03dcd72532f109953042af6"} {"question" "q-7945" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-7945" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-7945" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316768" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${A}^{-1},$ where\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316768" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $A$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(A)=5\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 0=-10\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-10}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1/5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1/2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{A}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1/5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1/2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {A}^{-1}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1/5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1/2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316768" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5afafdb2e5d49013b9bae6603b0bcc9b16798670b03dcd72532f109953042af6"} {"question" "q-316768" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316768" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316768" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316768" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316768" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316768" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316753" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${A}^{-1},$ where\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | $-2$ |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316753" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $A$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(A)=(-6)\\cdot 2-3\\cdot (-5)=3\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -(-5) & -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2/3 & -1 \\\\ 5/3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{A}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2/3 & -1 \\\\ 5/3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {A}^{-1}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2/3 & -1 \\\\ 5/3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316753" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5afafdb2e5d49013b9bae6603b0bcc9b16798670b03dcd72532f109953042af6"} {"question" "q-316753" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316753" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316753" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316753" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316753" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316753" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-7921" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${E}^{-1}$, where\n$E=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 7\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-7921" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $E$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(E)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(E)=4\\cdot 7-8\\cdot 3=4\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(E)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E{E}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {E}^{-1}E & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-7921" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5afafdb2e5d49013b9bae6603b0bcc9b16798670b03dcd72532f109953042af6"} {"question" "q-7921" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-7921" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 8 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 4\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-7921" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-11725" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-11725" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- The matrix $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=6\\cdot 4-8\\cdot 3=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)=0,$ we conclude that $B$ is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=(-1)\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 5=-10.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ do not have an inverse." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-11725" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5afafdb2e5d49013b9bae6603b0bcc9b16798670b03dcd72532f109953042af6"} {"question" "q-11725" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-11725" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$ and $B$ only"] ["text" "$A$ only"] ["text" "$A$, $B$, and $C$"] ["text" "$B$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$C$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-11725" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ and $B$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-71937" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -8 & 7 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -15 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-71937" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- The matrix $T$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $U$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(U)=3\\cdot 4-(-1)\\cdot (-15)=-3.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(U)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $U$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $V$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(V)=6\\cdot 5-10\\cdot 3=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(V)=0,$ we conclude that $V$ is not invertible. Since $V$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $V$ is singular.\n\nTherefore, only $V$ is singular." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-71937" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5afafdb2e5d49013b9bae6603b0bcc9b16798670b03dcd72532f109953042af6"} {"question" "q-71937" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-71937" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$T$ and $V$ only"] ["text" "$T$ only"] ["text" "$U$ and $V$ only"] ["text" "$U$ only"] ["text" "$V$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-71937" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$V$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-71938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 6 \\\\ 10 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,Y=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,Z=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-71938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- The matrix $X$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $Y$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Y)=6\\cdot 6-7\\cdot 5=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Y)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $Y$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $Z$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Z)=(-2)\\cdot 5-10\\cdot 1=-20.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Z)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $Z$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $X$ does not have an inverse." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-71938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5afafdb2e5d49013b9bae6603b0bcc9b16798670b03dcd72532f109953042af6"} {"question" "q-71938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-71938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$X$ and $Y$ only"] ["text" "$X$ and $Z$ only"] ["text" "$X$ only"] ["text" "$Y$ only"] ["text" "$Z$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-71938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$X$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-11718" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-11718" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the matrix $A$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 1=-1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(A)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=1\\cdot 0-0\\cdot 1=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)=0,$ we conclude that $C$ is not invertible. Since $C$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $C$ is singular.\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is singular." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-11718" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5afafdb2e5d49013b9bae6603b0bcc9b16798670b03dcd72532f109953042af6"} {"question" "q-11718" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-11718" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$ and $B$ only"] ["text" "$A$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$B$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$B$ only"] ["text" "$C$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-11718" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$C$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-127751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-127751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the matrix $A$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=(-1)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 0=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(A)=0,$ we conclude that $A$ is not invertible. Since $A$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $A$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=(-2)\\cdot 5-(-3)\\cdot (3)=-1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is singular." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-127751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5afafdb2e5d49013b9bae6603b0bcc9b16798670b03dcd72532f109953042af6"} {"question" "q-127751" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-127751" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$ and $B$ only"] ["text" "$A$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$A$ only"] ["text" "$B$ only"] ["text" "$C$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-127751" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-71968" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $H=[\\begin{aligned}5 & c \\\\ c & 5\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $c.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-71968" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $H$ is singular if and only if $det(H)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(H) & =5\\cdot 5-c\\cdot c \\\\  & =25-{c}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25-{c}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {c}^{2} & =25 \\\\ c & =\\pm 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $c$ are $c=\\pm 5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-71968" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5afafdb2e5d49013b9bae6603b0bcc9b16798670b03dcd72532f109953042af6"} {"question" "q-71968" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-71968" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "c=-5"] ["math" "c=5"] ["math" "c=6"] ["math" "c=\\pm 5"] ["math" "c=\\pm 6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-71968" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "c=\\pm 5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316784" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -x+1 \\\\ 5 & 2x+7\\end{aligned}]$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316784" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(-3)\\cdot (2x+7)-5\\cdot (-x+1) \\\\  & =-6x-21+5x-5 \\\\  & =-x-26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x-26 & =0 \\\\ -x & =26 \\\\ x & =-26\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316784" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5afafdb2e5d49013b9bae6603b0bcc9b16798670b03dcd72532f109953042af6"} {"question" "q-316784" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316784" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-26"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $B=[\\begin{aligned}2x+1 & x-40 \\\\ 1 & -x\\end{aligned}]$\nbe a singular matrix. **In ascending order**, the values of $x$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(2x+1)\\cdot (-x)-(x-40)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}-x-x+40 \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}-2x+40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2}-2x+40 & =0 \\\\ -2({x}^{2}+x-20) & =0 \\\\ -2(x-4)(x+5) & =0 \\\\ x & =4,-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the values of $x$ are\n\n$$\nx=-5\\,\\text{and}\\,x=4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5afafdb2e5d49013b9bae6603b0bcc9b16798670b03dcd72532f109953042af6"} {"question" "q-316828" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316828" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316828" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316828" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3x+2 & 2x-4\\end{aligned}]$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =1\\cdot (2x-4)-2\\cdot (3x+2) \\\\  & =2x-4-6x-4 \\\\  & =-4x-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x-8 & =0 \\\\ -4x & =8 \\\\ x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5afafdb2e5d49013b9bae6603b0bcc9b16798670b03dcd72532f109953042af6"} {"question" "q-316782" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316782" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $B=[\\begin{aligned}5x & -1 \\\\ 6x-8 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(5x)\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (6x-8) \\\\  & =10x+6x-8 \\\\  & =16x-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16x-8 & =0 \\\\ 16x & =8 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5afafdb2e5d49013b9bae6603b0bcc9b16798670b03dcd72532f109953042af6"} {"question" "q-316783" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "q-316783" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e7ad0e55e83a0bbad266f98f8e2beda5f48fe733ff2e6226737c5fd9c99a2a2"} {"question" "e-4502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $A^{-1},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/example-4502.json" "file_sha256" "d90d1dc48691d5c8e6cd79aaa9450e15416a1c0437b2e49a41de506ae4054a06"} {"question" "e-4502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a $2 \\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $A$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\det(A) = 1 \\cdot 1 - 0 \\cdot (-2) = 1\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}]. \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -0 \\\\ -(-2) & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{A}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {A}^{-1}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/example-4502.json" "file_sha256" "d90d1dc48691d5c8e6cd79aaa9450e15416a1c0437b2e49a41de506ae4054a06"} {"question" "e-4503" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/example-4503.json" "file_sha256" "c5231f1b59cd38e29c467d9e0c7ea837116f3d696d9cd56f0255d2f4b94f850c"} {"question" "e-4503" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the matrix $A$, we have\n\n$$\n\\det({A})=1 \\cdot 1 - 1 \\cdot 1 = 0.\n$$\n\nBecause $\\det(A)=0,$ we conclude that $A$ is not invertible. Since $A$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $A$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\n\\det({C})=3 \\cdot 3 - (-3) \\cdot 3 = 18.\n$$\n\nBecause $\\det(C) \\neq 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is singular." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/example-4503.json" "file_sha256" "c5231f1b59cd38e29c467d9e0c7ea837116f3d696d9cd56f0255d2f4b94f850c"} {"question" "e-4504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If \n$[\\begin{aligned}1-k & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1-k\\end{aligned}]$\n is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/example-4504.json" "file_sha256" "34fa14c36f2c4f3a517ce126819d1d70167f169e288fc03290cd6aa8867b1cee"} {"question" "e-4504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $\\det(A)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =(1-k)(1-k)-4 \\\\  & ={k}^{2}-2k-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $k\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{k}^{2}-2k-3 & =0 \\\\ (k-3)(k+1) & =0 \\\\ k & =3,-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $k$ are $k=3$ and $k=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039644/example-4504.json" "file_sha256" "34fa14c36f2c4f3a517ce126819d1d70167f169e288fc03290cd6aa8867b1cee"}] "usage" {"e-4503" [] "q-11725" [] "q-316782" [] "q-127742" [] "e-4502" [] "e-4504" [] "q-11718" [] "q-71938" []} "basis" 1376 "retractions" [[17592186087932 :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}6 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186084580 17592186084581 17592186084582 17592186084583 17592186084584 1